# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"A quantum-classical workflow runs as one managed workflow job. Its classical stages run on your compute profile, and the primitive jobs that it sends to an IBM Quantum&reg; QPU run on your instance and count against your usage. From that one job, you can report each stage, find the QPU jobs, and cancel them. To start a job and check its status and logs, see [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Un workflow cuántico-clásico se ejecuta como un único trabajo de workflow gestionado. Sus etapas clásicas se ejecutan en tu perfil de cómputo, y los trabajos de primitivas que envía a una QPU de IBM Quantum&reg; se ejecutan en tu instancia y cuentan para tu uso. Desde ese único trabajo, puedes informar de cada etapa, encontrar los trabajos de QPU y cancelarlos. Para iniciar un trabajo y consultar su estado y sus registros, consulta [Ejecutar un workflow gestionado](/guides/run-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [deploy your first managed workflow](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"
msgstr "Antes de empezar, [despliega tu primer workflow gestionado](/guides/deploy-first-managed-workflow).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service {#create-the-runtime-service}"
msgstr "Crear el servicio Runtime {#create-the-runtime-service}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the Runtime service in your workflow code with `get_runtime_service()`, and use it in the same way that you use `QiskitRuntimeService` locally. The following workflow runs a Bell circuit with the Sampler primitive, reports each stage with `update_status()`, and returns the counts:\n"
msgstr "Crea el servicio Runtime en el código de tu workflow con `get_runtime_service()` y úsalo del mismo modo que usas `QiskitRuntimeService` en local. El siguiente workflow ejecuta un circuito de Bell con la primitiva Sampler, informa de cada etapa con `update_status()` y devuelve los conteos:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_runtime_service()` returns a `QiskitRuntimeService` that is set up for your managed workflow job, and it provides the following:\n"
msgstr "`get_runtime_service()` devuelve un `QiskitRuntimeService` configurado para tu trabajo de workflow gestionado y ofrece lo siguiente:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Credentials.** The Runtime service uses the API key, instance, and channel that you used to call `run()`, so the workflow code needs no credentials.\n"
msgstr "**Credenciales.** El servicio Runtime usa la clave de API, la instancia y el canal que usaste para llamar a `run()`, así que el código del workflow no necesita credenciales.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Tracking.** A workflow records every primitive job that runs through this Runtime service under the managed workflow job, including Sampler, Estimator, and Executor jobs, and jobs in a session or batch. You can list them with `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "**Seguimiento.** Un workflow registra, bajo el trabajo de workflow gestionado, cada trabajo de primitiva que se ejecuta a través de este servicio Runtime, incluidos los trabajos de Sampler, Estimator y Executor, y los trabajos en una sesión o un batch. Puedes listarlos con `job.runtime_jobs()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Cancellation.** When you call `job.cancel()`, the managed workflow also cancels the workflow's sessions, batches, and primitive jobs that are still running.\n"
msgstr "**Cancelación.** Cuando llamas a `job.cancel()`, el workflow gestionado también cancela las sesiones, los batches y los trabajos de primitivas del workflow que aún se están ejecutando.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow does not track or cancel the jobs of a service that you create with `QiskitRuntimeService()`, although the jobs still run. If the workflow must use another service, cancel its jobs in a [`SIGTERM` handler](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"
msgstr "Un workflow gestionado no hace seguimiento ni cancela los trabajos de un servicio que creas con `QiskitRuntimeService()`, aunque los trabajos se sigan ejecutando. Si el workflow debe usar otro servicio, cancela sus trabajos en un [controlador de `SIGTERM`](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#clean-up-when-a-job-is-canceled).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run primitives in a session or batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"
msgstr "Ejecutar primitivas en una sesión o un batch {#run-primitives-in-a-session-or-batch}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow also tracks primitive jobs that run in a session or batch. Create the session or batch from a backend that the Runtime service returned, and create the primitives inside the `with` block. `Session` works in the same way:\n"
msgstr "Un workflow gestionado también hace seguimiento de los trabajos de primitivas que se ejecutan en una sesión o un batch. Crea la sesión o el batch a partir de un backend que devolvió el servicio Runtime y crea las primitivas dentro del bloque `with`. `Session` funciona del mismo modo:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"
msgstr "**`source_files/my_workflow.py`**\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Report progress with update_status() {#report-progress-with-update-status}"
msgstr "Informar del progreso con update_status() {#report-progress-with-update-status}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow in [Create the Runtime service](#create-the-runtime-service) calls `update_status()` at the start of each stage, so that the job status shows where the workflow is, such as `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Pass one of the following `Job` constants:\n"
msgstr "El workflow de [Crear el servicio Runtime](#create-the-runtime-service) llama a `update_status()` al inicio de cada etapa, de modo que el estado del trabajo muestra en qué punto está el workflow, por ejemplo `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU`. Pasa una de las siguientes constantes de `Job`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Call in the workflow | Job status |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Llamada en el workflow | Estado del trabajo |\n"
"| - | - |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.MAPPING)` | `RUNNING: MAPPING` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` | `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.WAITING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: WAITING_FOR_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.EXECUTING_QPU)` | `RUNNING: EXECUTING_QPU` |\n"
"| `update_status(Job.POST_PROCESSING)` | `RUNNING: POST_PROCESSING` |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status()` returns `True` if the workflow changed the status. It returns `False` and writes a warning to the logs if the value is not one of these constants, if the job is no longer active, or if the code runs outside a job. It does not raise an error, so a typo does not stop the workflow.\n"
msgstr "`update_status()` devuelve `True` si el workflow cambió el estado. Devuelve `False` y escribe una advertencia en los registros si el valor no es una de estas constantes, si el trabajo ya no está activo o si el código se ejecuta fuera de un trabajo. No lanza un error, así que un error tipográfico no detiene el workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For progress within a stage, such as the iterations of an optimizer, [write log lines](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"
msgstr "Para el progreso dentro de una etapa, como las iteraciones de un optimizador, [escribe líneas de registro](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors#best-practice-decide-what-to-log).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: each update_status() call writes a SUB_STATUS_CHANGE event, and the 24-hour timeout is measured from the job's latest event (update_fleets_jobs_statuses.py _timed_out). send_error() events count too. This looks like a bug; do not document it until the intended behavior is confirmed. */}\n"
msgstr ""

